2. In this Act, unless there is anything repugnant in
the subject or context‑‑‑
(a) "Academic Council" means the Academic
Council of the Institute;
(b) "Board" means the Board of Governors of
the Institute;
(c) "Chairman" means the Chairman of the
Board;
(d) "Director" means the Director of the
Institute;
(e) "Government"
means the Government of Sindh;
(f) "Institute" means
the Institute of Urology and Transplantation established under this Act;
(g) "Member" means a
Member of the Board;
(h) "Prescribed"
means prescribed by regulations framed under this Act;
(i) "Regulation"
means regulations made under this Act.

Power and duties of the board

ACT II OF 1991
ACT II OF 1991
SINDH INSTITUTE OF UROLOGY AND
TRANSPLANTATION ACT, 1991
7. Power and duties of the
Board.‑‑(1) The Board shall, subject to the provisions of this Act
and regulations, exercise administrative and financial powers in respect of the
Institute as may be necessary for its proper and efficient functioning;
(2) In particular and without prejudice to the
generality of the foregoing provision, the Board shall have the powers‑‑‑
(i) to hold, control and administer the property,
funds and resources the Institute and borrow or raise money for the purpose of
the Institute;
(ii) to exercise supervision
and overall control over the Institute;
(iii) to consider annual research programme, annual
reports and audited statements of accounts of the Institute;
(iv) to create, suspend or abolish such posts of
teaching and non‑teaching staff of the Institute as may be necessary;
(v) to appoint the Director;
(vi) to prescribe terms and conditions of the
teaching and non‑teaching staff of the Institute including the Director;
(vii) to consider and approve annual and revised
budget estimates and to re‑appropriate funds from one major head of
expenditure to another and to appoint auditors;
(viii) to cause proper books of accounts to be kept
for all sums of money received and expended by the Institute and for assets and
liabilities of the Institute;
(ix) to lay down its own rules
of procedure;
(x) to frame regulations;
(xi) to appoint committees or sub‑committees as
deemed fit for carrying out the purposes of this Act;
(xii) to delegate any of its powers to the Director,
excepting the approval of budgetary estimates.
